======================================================================
K=4 float-grid cross-check, n=6..2000 (integer) + geometric to 1e5
======================================================================
n values tested: 2002, violations: 0
worst ratio max|h4|/M4 = 0.9999695241291031 at n=100000

Note: for very large n (>~1e4-1e5), float64 catastrophic cancellation
(computing a ~1/n-scale quantity as a difference of ~n^6-n^8-scale terms)
starts eroding precision -- consistent with predecessor/target's own
disclosed finding about needing exact rational arithmetic for n up to 1e6+.
This script deliberately stays in a range (<=1e5) where float64's ~15-16
significant digits are still enough to be a meaningful (not misleading)
cross-check; it is a sanity net, not a load-bearing proof step, matching
both fronts' own stated role for this kind of check.
